E-Commerce Checkout: Payment Processing with Polymorphism

This is a Java project that simulates the payment part of an e-commerce checkout backend.
It supports credit card and PayPal payments and demonstrates runtime polymorphism (method overriding) together with method overloading

Project Structure

 File                             Description 

 `PaymentProcessor.java`     Parent class. Defines the generic `ProcessPayment` method (two forms) plus shared coupon and validation helpers. 
 `CreditCardProcessor.java`  Subclass. Overrides `ProcessPayment` with credit card logic (card validation + 2% fee).
 `PayPalProcessor.java`      Subclass. Overrides `ProcessPayment` with PayPal logic (email validation + 3% fee).
 `Main.java`                 Checkout simulation that runs both processors through a `PaymentProcessor` reference.

How Polymorphism Is Demonstrated

1. Runtime polymorphism (overriding).** Both subclasses override `ProcessPayment`.
In `Main`, every object is stored in a `PaymentProcessor` variable, but the object
is really a `CreditCardProcessor` or `PayPalProcessor`:

